ed and they were still in use when the war ended.","LocalizedString":"The Da 75/13 Modello 15 was a mountain gun from Austria-Hungary, originally known as the Skoda 75mm Model 15, but designated as the Obice da 75/13 in Italy. The Italians captured large numbers of these guns in WWI and they were distributed among the Italian Alpini divisions who found them very useful in mountain terrain. It was therefore decided to reproduce the Obice da 75/13 in 1933 and many of them were still in service when WWII started and they were still in use when the war ended."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardLeaveBoardOrOwner"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Alpine"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Artillery_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Artillery_Move_FX.0"},"soundMoveToFrontline":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Artillery_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Artillery_Move_FX.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'AU_Artillery_small_fire_01a'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Projectiles_and_Impacts/Artillery/AU_Artillery_small_fire_01a.0"},"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion02'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/StarterContent/Audio/Explosion02.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Italy/t_alpini_artillery.t_alpini_artillery","SubPathString":""},"artist":"David Pentland","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/OBICE_DA_75-13.OBICE_DA_75-13","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":291.0},"historyPhotoSource":"https://www.nevasport.com/fotos/051107/159186.jpg","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_unit_obice_da_75_13_photo","SourceString":"Obice Da 75/13 and crew, date unknown.","LocalizedString